{"id": "tea:jivanmuktiviveka:1", "source": "src:jivanmuktiviveka", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Renunciation is twofold: that of the seeker who desires to know (vividiṣā-sannyāsa), a means to knowledge, and that of the knower (vidvat-sannyāsa), a means to liberation while living.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:vividisa-sannyasa", "trm:vidvat-sannyasa"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-advaita"], "practices": ["prc:vividisa-sannyasa", "prc:vidvat-sannyasa"], "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jivanmuktiviveka:2-3", "source": "src:jivanmuktiviveka", "location": {"ref": "2-3"}, "paraphrase": "Knowledge of the truth, destruction of latent tendencies (vāsanā-kṣaya) and dissolution of the mind (mano-nāśa) are to be practised together, each supporting the others; without the latter two, knowledge does not bring the stable freedom of the jīvanmukta.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:vasana-ksaya", "trm:manonasa"], "concepts": ["cpt:vasanaksaya-manonasa"], "practices": ["prc:vasana-ksaya", "prc:manonasa"], "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jivanmuktiviveka:3", "source": "src:jivanmuktiviveka", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "The knower is graded by the seven stages of knowledge (from the Yoga Vāsiṣṭha): one at the fourth is a knower of Brahman; at the fifth, sixth and seventh, increasingly excellent knowers, distinguished by how far they rise from absorption by themselves or by others.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "karma-liberation"], "paths": ["pth:yoga-vasistha-seven-bhumikas"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukta-marks"], "cross_refs": ["tea:yoga-vasistha:3.118"], "notes": "Chapter placement and the cross-reference locator are low confidence.", "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jivanmuktiviveka:4", "source": "src:jivanmuktiviveka", "location": {"ref": "4"}, "paraphrase": "The purposes of liberation while living are five: protection of knowledge, austerity, absence of conflict, cessation of suffering, and the manifestation of bliss.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-purposes-of-jivanmukti"], "teachers": ["tch:vidyaranya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
